          dealing: 'Each player receives 4 cards (some variants 3). The remaining cards form the stock.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: "Capture at least 31 points (in a single round) or 61 points (if scores are combined) to win. Avoid getting zero points ('The Goat').",
          gameplay: '1. **Multiple Lead**: You can lead one card, two of a suit, or three of a suit.\n2. **Response**: Subsequent players MUST play the same number of cards.\n3. **Trumping**: Any card in a lead can be beaten by a higher card of the same suit or a Trump card.\n4. **Capturing**: To win the trick, a player must beat ALL cards led with individual higher cards.\n5. **Drawing**: After a trick, everyone draws from stock back to 4 cards.',
          keyRules: [
            'Lead one to four cards of the same suit.',
            'Followers must play the same number of cards.',
            'No obligation to follow suit; beat with higher card of same suit or any trump.',
            'To win a trick, beat every led card with a higher card.',
            'After each trick, players draw from stock to refill to four cards.',
            'Declarations (Bura, Moskva, Molodka) may seize the lead.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Conserve your Tens and Aces for 'Multi-Leads'. If you lead two 10s at once, the opponent must produce two cards to beat them, which is statistically difficult.",
          intermediate: "Stock Management: Always keep a Trump card in your hand to defend against a 'Bura' declaration. If you are 'void' of trumps, you are a vulnerable target for multi-card leads.",
          advanced: "The 'Goat' Trap: If you see an opponent has no tricks by the halfway point, lead low non-scoring cards to prevent them from winning anything. If they end with zero tricks, they take double penalty points (The Full Goat).",
          tips: [
            'Diamonds are traditionally trumps in Kozel, though house rules may vary.',
            "If you have a 'Bura' (3 trumps), don't play it immediately. Wait until the opponent leads a high-scoring 10 or Ace to capture it.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
